            "minimumOsVersion": "14.0",
            "releaseNotes": "Resolved Issues: \n\u2022  Mail: The unread-count badge in the Dock now initializes correctly at startup.  \n\u2022  Mail: Improved the experience for viewing and interacting with Loop components in Outlook messages.\n\u2022  Add-ins: Attachments added or removed by add-ins now synchronize more reliably, including during rapid or overlapping draft saves. \n \nFeature Updates: \n\u2022  Calendar: Outlook Settings now let users manage work hours and work-location schedules for supported accounts.\n\u2022  Calendar: Users can choose whether accepted invitations are removed from the Inbox and whether conflicting events are automatically declined on supported accounts.\n\u2022  Mail: Replies forwards, initial content, and signatures now automatically follow the left-to-right or right-to-left direction of the referenced message.\n\u2022  Mail: Added Editor Settings to customize spelling and grammar by language. \n\u2022  Mail: Added a remove button to make deleting recipients easier when composing emails. \n\u2022  Mail: Paste Options now supports converting Markdown to rich text. \n\u2022  Mail: Paragraph Options now provide better control over advanced formatting.\n\u2022  Contacts: Administrators can use cloud policy to control whether presence indicators appear for recipients and contacts in Outlook.\n\u2022  Copilot: Eligible users can now see linked Microsoft account subscriptions associated with their Copilot account in Outlook Settings. \n\u2022  Security: Outlook can automatically inherit an appropriate sensitivity label from labeled attachments \n\u2022  General: Users can right-click Mail, Calendar, and People icons in the left rail to open them in a separate window. \n\u2022  General: Users can personalize Outlook by choosing an accent color.",
            "version": "16.113",
            "app_store_url": "https://apps.apple.com/us/app/microsoft-outlook/id985367838?mt=12&uo=4"
        },
